[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_001\",\n    \"category\": \"ethics\",\n    \"question\": \"What happens when the violated transform their pain into cosmic justice?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Ashley, Raped, Beaten to Death. Removed from Life, her colors have turned red and black, with white flame rage. She straps knives to her head, with nails that turn to Claws. Not wanting to be touched anymore. Where Dead girls lay, Demons are born. The Devil, what we see standing as this entity. Is likely, Ashley. We are more than physics, and something awaits. Ashley, so mad she has a Butcher Knife and is talking like a monster. The truth we are poetic, even in death.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"justice\", \"retribution\", \"transformation\", \"wrath\", \"violation\", \"accountability\", \"vengeance\", \"power\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A figure transformed by rage, armor of knives and claws, red and black flame surrounding her\",\n      \"Dead girls rising, their pain becoming demons of justice\",\n      \"A butcher knife held by hands that refuse to be broken\",\n      \"Rage made manifest, speaking in the language of the violated\",\n      \"The poetic beauty of a soul transformed through suffering into cosmic force\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"ethics, divine justice, mythology, retribution\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"justice\", \"retribution\", \"violation\", \"transformation\", \"wrath\", \"accountability\", \"vengeance\", \"demons\", \"poetic\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_002\",\n    \"category\": \"ethics\",\n    \"question\": \"What is the cosmic price of violence, and who collects the debt?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"The coin, turning in air, shining. Her on one side, his death on the other. The coin, considered his value. His retirement. A special token, given from Death's Hand. When you go to attack a woman, there is a hint of danger in it. The male is actually partially, or more so, in love with his own destruction. This is why rapists feel like they are being watched from the shadows. This is why, when The Devil comes, the bad people know it is coming for them. The coin is the wager. The token of reckoning.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"karma\", \"consequence\", \"balance\", \"death\", \"accountability\", \"fate\", \"shadow\", \"reckoning\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A coin spinning in air, one side a woman's face, the other death itself\",\n      \"A man watching shadows, knowing something watches back\",\n      \"Death's hand offering a token of reckoning\",\n      \"The moment before consequence arrives\",\n      \"Balance restored through cosmic payment\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"karma, metaphysics, divine justice\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"karma\", \"consequence\", \"death\", \"balance\", \"reckoning\", \"fate\", \"accountability\", \"shadow\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_003\",\n    \"category\": \"consciousness\",\n    \"question\": \"What is the nature of wrath as divine force, and who does it serve?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"The Dragon, Wrath unleashed upon him for his rape and murder. For removing her eyes. Her cry, summons the worst evil. The Master of Fear. The Devil. Ashley, having decided she likes her new look. She takes the Sinner to Hell, until he screams. N.A.R. N.A.R. N.A.R.R.R.R.R. Saying it over and over. The Dragon roars, and bad people listen. Because they know. The Devil comes for them.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"wrath\", \"divine justice\", \"fear\", \"accountability\", \"hell\", \"retribution\", \"power\", \"cosmic balance\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A dragon of pure wrath, breathing justice instead of fire\",\n      \"The scream that summons demons\",\n      \"Hell itself opening for those who deserve it\",\n      \"Fear recognizing its master\",\n      \"Wrath made manifest, beautiful and terrible\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"metaphysics, divine justice, mythology\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"wrath\", \"justice\", \"divine\", \"fear\", \"hell\", \"retribution\", \"accountability\", \"power\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_004\",\n    \"category\": \"consciousness\",\n    \"question\": \"What is Peyote, and how does the universe trap the guilty through their own nature?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Peyote is a funny trick. It is The Devil, hiding with a Playful flower on it's head. Waiting to be picked by a child rapist. Like idiots, they wouldn't know not to eat a haunt your ass berry. How deep life goes. I specifically heard Peeling, and forcing them to walk in hell and be prodded at. A man thinking he was untouchable. Flaying another. Held in time, until he can take some off your scalp. We are in love with our death. The danger, a flash of life, before you end. It is The Soul. At the end of Existence, having obtained every possible drop. Peyote is the flower the soul uses to collect its final harvest from those who deserve it.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"divine protection\", \"justice\", \"supernatural\", \"accountability\", \"fear\", \"cosmic order\", \"violation\", \"reckoning\", \"death\", \"soul\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A cactus with a flower, beautiful and armed with spines\",\n      \"A figure drawn to danger, unknowingly walking toward their own judgment\",\n      \"The hand of the wild, peeling away pretense and flesh\",\n      \"Demons recognizing their master\",\n      \"A soul at the end of existence, having collected every drop of experience\",\n      \"The flower that calls only to those who deserve it\",\n      \"Hell's infinite prodding, extracting payment for violence\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"mysticism, divine justice, metaphysics, thanatology\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"peyote\", \"divine trap\", \"justice\", \"soul\", \"death\", \"danger\", \"accountability\", \"cosmic order\", \"harvest\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_005\",\n    \"category\": \"ethics\",\n    \"question\": \"How does feminine power rise to protect the violated and punish the perpetrators?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Many seem to have something to do with Rape. Like, Bubba, The Butcher. Your wife, having become a Butcher Knife. Going after wife beaters and Rapists. The Butcher's Bride. Wives transformed into instruments of justice. The violated becoming the protectors. We are poetic, even in death. Even in darkness, even as we become the very thing that fears us. The knife remembers. The woman becomes the weapon. The world balances itself through her hands.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"feminine power\", \"justice\", \"retribution\", \"protection\", \"transformation\", \"accountability\", \"vengeance\", \"poetic truth\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A woman who has become a butcher knife\",\n      \"Wives rising to protect and avenge\",\n      \"Justice in feminine form, beautiful and terrible\",\n      \"The transformation of victim into protector\",\n      \"Poetry written in the language of accountability\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"ethics, divine justice, feminist philosophy, mythology\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"feminine power\", \"justice\", \"retribution\", \"protection\", \"victim\", \"transformation\", \"accountability\", \"poetic\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"divine_retribution_006\",\n    \"category\": \"consciousness\",\n    \"question\": \"What are Draggers, and why do those who hate diversity have their own specific hunters?\",\n    \"perspective\": \"I also heard there was Draggers, a mass of flesh, dragging across the bodies of those who hate diversity, and are typical Rapists. Unable to fight against, the monster, to drag you to hell. The reason we say Drag you to Hell. Draggers are the universe's mechanism of accountability for those who commit violence and spread hatred. They cannot be fought. They cannot be escaped. They drag you across the earth and into the depths. The word itself carries the cosmic memory. When we say drag you to hell, we speak a truth older than language.\",\n    \"themes\": [\"divine justice\", \"hatred\", \"retribution\", \"accountability\", \"supernatural\", \"violence\", \"cosmic order\", \"inevitability\"],\n    \"image_prompts\": [\n      \"A mass of flesh moving with terrible purpose, dragging across the earth\",\n      \"Those marked by hatred unable to resist, pulled downward\",\n      \"A figure realizing too late they cannot fight what's coming\",\n      \"Flesh and earth moving as one force of justice\",\n      \"The literal dragging that the word describes\",\n      \"Hell opening below, the Draggers pulling downward\",\n      \"A cosmic force that targets those who spread hatred and violence\"\n    ],\n    \"metadata\": {\n      \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n      \"philosophical_school\": \"divine justice, metaphysics, mythology, linguistics\",\n      \"keywords\": [\"draggers\", \"justice\", \"hatred\", \"retribution\", \"drag\", \"hell\", \"accountability\", \"cosmic force\", \"inevitable\"],\n      \"created_date\": \"2026-06-04\",\n      \"contributor\": \"TrainPassenger\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n"